<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> Yes<br />
<strong>Page Type:</strong> Scp Article<br />
<strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Scp 5133 gets contained for an anomaly that has is blocked by personnel, as any description of appearance or behavior will cause the people involved to worship Scp 5133.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Site 138 staff had all fallen into Scp 5133's memetic ability, no replies had been filed to site fund managers, two mtf operatives go to try to contain any escaped anomaly's after believing that site 138 had suffered a containment breach. They arrive and all scp's are contained except Scp 5133 where they report that it is memetic. Perfect containment cant be made as the original anomoly can be discovered and cared for if no information can be learnt.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The archived containment procedures are not what anyone would expect, as it states any personnel showing disliking to Scp 5133 are to be terminated via incinerator, and the archived description has been blocked by upper site command.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Site 138 is just a random number I picked so finding a site that stores anomalies that could have been corrupted by a memetic hazard. And a site that can house things you dont know.</p>

