<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article. Several experimental test logs added as well.</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Sci-fi, Parallel Universes</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX is a computer program that one day appeared and automatically installed in every computer at site-XX. If run it will display the message &quot;SCP Breach Simulator- Site XX Edition&quot; and then create a realistic simulation of site XX, were you will play as yourself and will have to survive a SCP breach.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Any computer brought into site-XX will manifest the program inside of their files, even if the computer was completely cut out from the internet and any other method of networking. SCP-XXXX cannot be deleted but any computer that is taken outside of the site will have the program erased from its files. SCP-XXXX will work on personal computers and laptops; smartphones, tablets, servers and mainframes won't manifest the program inside of their files. On the other hand anything that classifies as a personal computer, regardless of its model, year of manufacture or Operating System will manifest and be able to run the program. Older models will create more crude simulations, with very old computers generating text based descriptions and allowing the users to chose how to act with input prompts and more modern computers generating 3D environment that can even be compatible with Virtual Reality technology.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> The program manifested after a particularly sudden and gruesome containment breach. In that breach agent XXXX mentioned how it felt as if her actions were not her own, but chosen and forced upon her by someone else. It is believed that the simulations that the SCP generates are not simulations at all, but live feed from a parallel universe where a breach is occurring. Players from this universe take control of their versions from the universe that is being shown in the computer, and the simulation will run until the breach is contained, the SCP escapes or the &quot;player&quot; dies. It is believed that after running a simulation SCP-XXXX will automatically install in every computer of site-XX of that particular parallel universe, spreading itself further and further.</p>
<p>The foundation can choose to use the SCP to conduct breaching simulations or even spy in parallel universes and steal research or information that might help their cause, but at the cost of damaging another SCP foundation from a parallel universe and spreading the SCP more and more. The more the SCP has spread the higher the chances are for the Foundation of this universe from becoming another &quot;simulation&quot; and suffering a breach.</p>
</div>
