<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Documents, people, writings, anything infected with the SCP becomes very unnaturally vague, but doesn't cause any other harmful side effect.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The phenomena is referred to as &quot;Vagueing&quot; or &quot;The Vague&quot;.</p>
<p>The SCP isn't a state of matter, nor does it exist physically, rather it's a strange unknown phenomena that spreads from person to person, only when they share ideas, brainstorm together, etc. It effects a person's speaking, and causes them to speak rather vague.</p>
<p>Not only does it effect humans, but also effects documents and anything written by &quot;Vagued Men&quot;. Such infected manuscripts include a lost SCP-001 article, and the &quot;11th&quot; commandment. It has the same exact effects, causing very slurred and vague text.</p>
<p>The SCP does not have any other side effects, and only causes slurring in speech, and unnatural vagueness, no nausea, no coughing, no death, nothing like that.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> Basic idea yet has a lot of interesting details when it comes to &quot;documents lost to the vague&quot;.</p>

